WEBVTT

00:48.131 --> 00:49.632
Easy, little guy.

01:12.155 --> 01:13.782
What's he doing?

01:36.554 --> 01:37.889
You wanna live?

01:51.861 --> 01:53.071
I'm just…

01:54.614 --> 01:55.990
I wanna die in here.

01:58.868 --> 01:59.911
Yeah?

02:01.621 --> 02:02.664
I get it.

02:37.699 --> 02:39.409
Thank you for this meal.

03:12.984 --> 03:14.819
LIFE IN THE WOODS
BY HENRY DAVID THOREAU

05:01.259 --> 05:02.885
It's so beautiful.

05:05.013 --> 05:06.264
Yes.

05:08.766 --> 05:10.059
Dad…

05:12.812 --> 05:14.605
Let's say there really was a God.

05:15.523 --> 05:17.191
What would you ask for?

05:19.610 --> 05:20.945
Aah…

05:23.072 --> 05:24.282
Hmm…

05:27.744 --> 05:30.621
That there would be
more mountains for us to climb!

05:30.705 --> 05:33.082
Where no human being has ever been.

05:33.166 --> 05:34.083
Please, dear God!

05:38.129 --> 05:39.922
You're crazy.

05:41.466 --> 05:45.803
Mountains like that don't exist
in the world today, Yuzuha.

05:47.347 --> 05:48.181
Your turn, now.

05:54.020 --> 05:56.522
I want this moment to last forever!

06:03.571 --> 06:04.822
A mountaintop…

06:05.990 --> 06:07.200
is where I…

06:09.285 --> 06:12.205
A mountaintop is
where I can really be myself.

06:14.374 --> 06:16.834
Dad, you are the only one

06:17.418 --> 06:20.338
who makes me believe
that I have a place in this world.

06:25.510 --> 06:27.887
I wanna live this moment forever.

06:32.392 --> 06:33.810
You'd get bored.

06:49.492 --> 06:50.785
That's his daughter!

06:50.868 --> 06:53.538
- There she is!
- Ms. Usagi! Ms. Usagi!

06:55.957 --> 06:58.376
- I just wanna ask you…
- Did he actually climb Mount Everest?

06:58.459 --> 07:00.670
Is it true that your father didn't
actually make the climb

07:00.753 --> 07:01.587
that he said he did?

07:01.671 --> 07:04.048
Please… Ms. Usagi, Ms. Usagi, over here!

07:04.132 --> 07:06.175
Please comment, please!

07:07.927 --> 07:09.053
Welcome home.

07:12.390 --> 07:13.307
Dad.

07:14.892 --> 07:16.185
Don't you worry.

07:16.978 --> 07:19.021
I don't know who's spreading these lies,

07:19.939 --> 07:21.691
but I've always told you the truth.

07:29.365 --> 07:30.783
Where are you going?

07:31.784 --> 07:32.869
To the mountain.

07:48.301 --> 07:49.385
Dad, wait.

07:53.639 --> 07:54.724
The mountain…

07:55.892 --> 07:58.227
is where I can really be myself.

08:23.628 --> 08:27.131
STAGED?

08:27.215 --> 08:30.134
SOLO NO-OXYGEN MOUNTAIN CLIMBING
SUSPECTED TO BE STAGED

08:30.218 --> 08:32.637
HE USED AN OXYGEN SUPPLEMENT

08:32.720 --> 08:35.640
IT WAS AN IMPOSSIBLE CHALLENGE
IN THE FIRST PLACE

08:35.723 --> 08:39.018
DID USAGI STAGE THE ENTIRE EVENT?

08:39.101 --> 08:42.146
550-STRONG SEARCH PARTY
LOOK FOR MISSING CLIMBER

08:42.230 --> 08:48.903
NO CLUES ON HIS WHEREABOUTS

08:48.986 --> 08:51.447
WORLD-FAMOUS MOUNTAINEER MISSING

08:51.531 --> 08:53.157
DID SHIGENORI USAGI
COMMIT SUICIDE

08:53.241 --> 08:55.159
DUE TO SUSPICIONS
ON STAGED MOUNTAIN CLIMBING?

08:55.243 --> 08:58.871
SUICIDE

10:02.059 --> 10:03.477
Thank you for the meal.

10:17.450 --> 10:18.826
Why did you save me?

10:31.047 --> 10:33.424
Your body says, "I want to live."

10:36.177 --> 10:37.428
My body?

10:41.390 --> 10:43.267
Might say it wants to live…

10:49.774 --> 10:52.693
But I don't deserve to live anymore.

10:57.615 --> 10:59.158
They're all dead.

11:02.620 --> 11:04.955
And I'm the only one still alive.

11:08.292 --> 11:11.170
They all had to die so I could survive.

11:15.675 --> 11:18.302
I might as well have been the one
who killed them all.

11:21.180 --> 11:23.391
I killed them all.

11:26.519 --> 11:29.021
I don't deserve to live.

11:29.647 --> 11:32.108
Not after I let them all die.

11:35.152 --> 11:36.654
I have to die.

11:38.698 --> 11:40.032
I have to die.

11:41.450 --> 11:42.868
I have to die!

11:45.246 --> 11:47.456
I have to die to be with them.

11:49.083 --> 11:53.629
I need to die!
I need to make it up to all of them!

11:54.755 --> 11:58.134
I need to make amends
for everything I've done!

12:07.935 --> 12:09.687
Why?

12:12.565 --> 12:13.733
Why?

12:20.740 --> 12:21.741
I…

12:25.494 --> 12:26.829
I'm hungry.

12:33.502 --> 12:34.712
I understand.

12:35.796 --> 12:38.007
There was a time I wanted to die too.

12:43.429 --> 12:44.722
Just like you do.

12:47.349 --> 12:49.268
I was just laying on the ground.

12:50.978 --> 12:52.980
And I started feeling hungry.

12:59.445 --> 13:01.155
I know one day, I will die.

13:04.992 --> 13:07.828
And it could be
when we're playing the game tomorrow

13:08.496 --> 13:10.372
or when my visa expires.

13:17.630 --> 13:19.340
But for now, I made that food.

13:21.217 --> 13:23.010
So eat it while you're still alive.

14:50.598 --> 14:51.599
Get ready.

14:56.228 --> 14:57.938
You've got a game to play.

15:03.444 --> 15:05.613
Are you planning to die
by having your visa expire?

15:18.542 --> 15:20.377
That time you screamed at all of us.

15:27.426 --> 15:28.969
During the tag game…

15:32.389 --> 15:34.850
You risked your life
trying to save everyone.

15:35.976 --> 15:37.102
- Everyone!
- Hey!

15:37.186 --> 15:39.813
He's up here! Over here,
he's on the second level!

15:39.897 --> 15:42.066
Tell us where he is if you see him!

15:42.149 --> 15:44.068
And let's all look for the symbol!

15:49.323 --> 15:50.991
I didn't wanna die then.

15:57.247 --> 15:59.333
And I didn't want anyone else too, either.

16:04.254 --> 16:05.673
I know what you're saying.

16:07.466 --> 16:09.385
And I don't want you to die now.

16:12.972 --> 16:16.475
If you hadn't screamed back there,
I'd be dead now.

16:27.486 --> 16:28.862
Let me repay you.

17:06.817 --> 17:08.944
THIS WAY TO THE GAME ARENA

17:09.028 --> 17:10.279
THIS WAY TO THE GAME ARENA

17:10.362 --> 17:13.949
THE GAME ARENA IS UP AHEAD

17:14.033 --> 17:16.368
THIS WAY TO THE GAME ARENA

18:53.882 --> 18:55.425
1 PER PERSON

19:06.311 --> 19:09.106
FACE RECOGNITION IN PROGRESS
PLEASE WAIT FOR A MOMENT

19:10.566 --> 19:12.109
You're not newbies.

19:14.778 --> 19:16.029
And who are you?

19:17.322 --> 19:19.408
We're the guys
who cleared four games together.

19:20.367 --> 19:23.871
We met at the first game
and now we work together as a team.

19:24.997 --> 19:28.500
But we might need more
if we're gonna clear this one.

19:31.253 --> 19:33.172
And your leg? Are you hurt?

19:35.799 --> 19:38.969
Ah… I tweaked it a bit.

19:40.304 --> 19:41.471
In the game?

19:44.600 --> 19:45.684
Yeah.

19:50.606 --> 19:52.274
Okay, the game's starting.

19:52.357 --> 19:54.735
Registration is now closed.

19:54.818 --> 19:57.112
The game is about to commence.

19:57.196 --> 19:59.448
Difficulty, Four of Clubs.

19:59.531 --> 20:02.701
There are a total of five participants.

20:02.784 --> 20:04.411
Game, "Distance".

20:04.494 --> 20:06.413
"Distance"?

20:06.997 --> 20:11.293
Rule. Endure the trial
while striving for the goal 

20:11.376 --> 20:12.878
within the time limit.

20:13.712 --> 20:14.796
Clear condition.

20:15.380 --> 20:17.466
Safely attain the goal.

20:18.050 --> 20:19.218
What is this?

20:19.718 --> 20:21.470
The game will now commence.

20:22.054 --> 20:24.932
120 minutes remaining.

20:27.976 --> 20:29.770
Does this mean we have to run?

20:31.021 --> 20:32.397
What do you think, Seizan?

20:35.400 --> 20:36.526
"Distance"?

20:37.778 --> 20:38.904
Zero.

20:41.782 --> 20:44.243
We have to run? On the highway?

20:46.536 --> 20:48.288
Uh, run?

20:48.372 --> 20:50.582
Takuma. Just relax.

20:51.875 --> 20:53.210
Sit down, sit down.

20:54.002 --> 20:56.922
I think these old buses
from the '70s all have V8 engines.

21:00.133 --> 21:02.010
Let's hope it starts.

21:02.094 --> 21:04.137
Come on, baby!

21:08.267 --> 21:09.977
Shit! It's out of gas.

21:11.520 --> 21:13.230
Looks like we have to run.

21:19.653 --> 21:20.862
Go on. Leave me here.

21:28.704 --> 21:30.747
- Takuma!
- Listen to me.

21:31.623 --> 21:34.793
I don't plan to just sit on my ass here,
roll over, and die.

21:36.962 --> 21:39.131
I'm gonna try to find a way to survive.

21:40.882 --> 21:42.175
But you gotta go.

21:46.513 --> 21:49.016
- We're not leaving you behind!
- Yamane!

21:51.184 --> 21:53.395
You gotta survive, so go now!

21:54.604 --> 21:56.398
You wanna see your wife again, right?

21:57.441 --> 21:59.860
And what about that baby she's carrying?

22:02.070 --> 22:04.614
What the hell are they supposed to do
without you?

22:11.455 --> 22:14.499
Don't worry about me. I got this.

22:23.508 --> 22:24.593
Yamane.

22:26.470 --> 22:27.721
Let's go.

22:32.934 --> 22:33.977
Go on.

22:35.937 --> 22:36.813
Now.

22:37.731 --> 22:38.899
You can do this.

22:48.742 --> 22:49.993
Let's go.

22:58.627 --> 22:59.711
Let's go.

23:10.263 --> 23:11.932
He made the right choice.

23:22.442 --> 23:25.153
110 minutes remaining.

23:50.929 --> 23:52.097
Arisu.

23:52.180 --> 23:53.348
Live for us.

23:53.932 --> 23:55.183
Thank you.

24:23.503 --> 24:25.297
Distance, 1,000.

24:34.723 --> 24:37.851
90 minutes remaining.

24:39.269 --> 24:40.562
To reach the goal,

24:41.480 --> 24:43.440
how much further do we have to run?

24:55.452 --> 24:58.872
Distance, 5,000.

25:05.670 --> 25:06.630
Hey.

25:07.422 --> 25:08.632
What's that?

25:15.013 --> 25:16.932
REPLENISHMENT STATION

25:22.354 --> 25:23.647
We made it.

25:31.738 --> 25:32.614
Wait.

25:32.697 --> 25:34.533
- Hang on a sec.
- Eh?

25:37.536 --> 25:39.287
You're waiting for us to drink it,
aren't you?

25:42.666 --> 25:43.959
No, we're not.

25:52.384 --> 25:53.552
Drink this.

25:54.761 --> 25:55.679
Thank you.

26:07.857 --> 26:09.025
That was great.

26:17.534 --> 26:18.785
Are you sure?

26:19.661 --> 26:20.662
Uh-huh.

26:38.888 --> 26:41.808
Distance, 6,000.

26:43.810 --> 26:46.313
Man, it's dark in here.

26:53.612 --> 26:57.741
Shit, this isn't Clubs.
It's gotta be a game of Spades.

27:01.369 --> 27:02.954
Something's over there.

27:10.920 --> 27:12.297
I don't see anything.

27:12.881 --> 27:14.883
Yeah. Right there.

27:33.485 --> 27:34.569
Run!

29:25.138 --> 29:28.558
Oh my god, oh my god. Help me!

29:36.775 --> 29:38.026
Help!

29:39.110 --> 29:42.155
No! Get off!

29:42.238 --> 29:43.323
Seizan!

29:43.406 --> 29:44.866
- Let's go!
- Come on!

29:44.949 --> 29:45.784
Get off!

29:48.703 --> 29:51.164
Seizan! Seizan!

29:56.085 --> 29:58.588
- I can't run anymore.
- Come on!

30:02.342 --> 30:03.426
I'm done.

30:06.846 --> 30:07.847
I can't.

30:14.062 --> 30:15.522
I'd only been with them…

30:16.815 --> 30:18.358
for about a week, but…

30:21.402 --> 30:23.071
it's like I knew them both…

30:24.489 --> 30:26.241
for my entire life.

30:34.958 --> 30:36.334
You gotta live.

30:37.001 --> 30:38.837
So you can tell your wife about them.

30:49.722 --> 30:50.723
You're right.

31:03.778 --> 31:06.948
Distance, 8,000.

31:22.005 --> 31:23.089
What are you doing?

31:24.090 --> 31:25.133
A motorcycle.

31:27.760 --> 31:29.387
Royal Enfield.

31:31.514 --> 31:32.765
You know bikes?

31:34.392 --> 31:36.227
Diesel engines like that are pretty rare.

31:40.899 --> 31:43.192
But old stuff like this still works

31:43.276 --> 31:46.195
since none of it has any IC chips.

31:48.698 --> 31:49.699
Hang on.

31:50.491 --> 31:51.951
Electronics.

31:53.077 --> 31:55.872
All electrical circuits
have been destroyed.

31:56.956 --> 31:57.790
So?

31:57.874 --> 32:01.044
Analog stuff
with no electrical circuitry still works.

32:01.127 --> 32:03.379
All motorcycles and all the cars
still work.

32:03.463 --> 32:06.382
Like this bike, or that bus back there!

32:11.095 --> 32:12.805
Damn it, no battery.

32:15.183 --> 32:18.061
This bike, you said it's got
an old diesel engine, right?

32:18.144 --> 32:19.187
Uh-huh.

32:19.270 --> 32:21.648
So it doesn't run on regular gas,
but diesel.

32:22.231 --> 32:24.317
- So does the bus, nice!
- Uh-huh.

32:25.735 --> 32:27.570
Wait, so…

32:27.654 --> 32:30.239
You want to carry that bike
all the way back with you?

32:30.323 --> 32:33.910
If we get this fuel back there,
we can use the bus and save Takuma.

32:33.993 --> 32:35.703
You wanna save Takuma?

32:35.787 --> 32:37.455
- Uh-huh.
- But if we go back,

32:37.538 --> 32:39.290
then the game can't be cleared!

32:39.374 --> 32:41.751
Yes it can. There's still enough time.

32:42.502 --> 32:44.754
But just in case, you two keep going.

32:44.837 --> 32:47.632
If I can start that bus,
I'll catch up real fast.

32:48.925 --> 32:51.219
No more surviving
by letting other people die.

32:52.220 --> 32:53.262
I'm done with it.

33:13.574 --> 33:16.995
Distance, 7,000.

33:22.291 --> 33:25.545
Distance, 10,000.

33:36.681 --> 33:39.100
Distance, 6,000.

33:39.851 --> 33:43.438
Distance, 12,000.

33:48.526 --> 33:52.071
Distance, 4,000.

34:05.293 --> 34:06.252
What?

34:08.588 --> 34:09.630
That's the goal.

34:13.009 --> 34:15.470
All right, let's wait for them.

34:23.561 --> 34:26.773
Distance, 1,000.

34:31.194 --> 34:34.864
15 minutes remaining.

34:37.283 --> 34:38.576
Hey!

34:46.834 --> 34:48.127
Hey!

34:57.053 --> 34:58.429
Hey!

35:11.984 --> 35:15.696
ENTRY PROHIBITED

35:24.080 --> 35:25.206
Your wife?

35:32.421 --> 35:35.091
This autumn, we're expecting a baby.

35:45.852 --> 35:48.020
I'm sure
they're waiting for you somewhere.

35:53.818 --> 35:54.944
Somewhere…

35:57.321 --> 35:58.447
they're waiting.

36:01.826 --> 36:03.661
Everyone's waiting.

36:08.666 --> 36:10.543
They're all out there somewhere.

36:18.718 --> 36:20.720
So you have to stay alive to see them.

36:33.149 --> 36:36.027
Five minutes remaining.

36:36.569 --> 36:38.112
Doesn't look like they made it.

36:45.411 --> 36:46.829
What the hell was that?

36:51.542 --> 36:53.044
What is that?

37:02.762 --> 37:03.679
Water?

37:55.022 --> 37:56.232
I can't run anymore!

37:56.315 --> 37:58.818
Yes, you can! Don't look back!

38:01.862 --> 38:02.822
Ah!

38:27.763 --> 38:28.848
Usagi!

38:36.314 --> 38:37.398
Arisu!

39:24.737 --> 39:26.655
Arisu.

39:49.720 --> 39:50.971
Oh, it hurts.

39:54.517 --> 39:55.810
Are you all right?

40:10.866 --> 40:12.785
Thank you. Thanks.

40:34.432 --> 40:35.724
Goal.

40:37.935 --> 40:39.603
So this whole time…

40:41.689 --> 40:43.315
I was at the goal?

40:46.861 --> 40:49.530
It was right there for us to see.

40:49.613 --> 40:52.491
The bus was the goal from the very start.

40:53.659 --> 40:56.328
Then what were all those numbers about?

40:56.412 --> 40:57.955
The distance to the goal.

40:59.373 --> 41:00.916
We were safe at zero.

41:09.925 --> 41:11.510
Game cleared.

41:11.594 --> 41:13.888
Congratulations.

41:19.226 --> 41:20.436
I got you.

41:34.617 --> 41:36.494
Hey, wait! Where are you going?

41:43.334 --> 41:44.502
I, uh…

41:46.504 --> 41:47.838
I have no idea.

41:56.138 --> 41:57.640
But I hope that…

42:01.519 --> 42:03.229
we'll meet again.

42:33.676 --> 42:35.052
The Beach?

42:36.178 --> 42:38.889
Maybe the people
who disappeared are there.

42:38.973 --> 42:41.892
Could it be
some kind of evacuation shelter?

42:42.518 --> 42:43.894
Yeah, maybe.

42:45.271 --> 42:47.064
But there's an answer out there.

42:49.525 --> 42:51.735
And I wanna remember Karube's words.

42:54.071 --> 42:55.614
I'm gonna do it for everyone.

42:57.283 --> 42:59.827
I'm gonna find the mastermind
of this sick game.

43:00.911 --> 43:02.955
And get this world back to the way it was.

43:05.499 --> 43:06.584
I swear it.

43:10.504 --> 43:14.216
But to do that,
I have to head to the Beach.

43:40.576 --> 43:42.411
You really don't know how to ride a bike?

43:43.245 --> 43:44.496
I never learned how.

43:45.122 --> 43:46.915
That's pretty hard to believe.

43:51.337 --> 43:53.339
But this feels nice.
